WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.420
You've probably seen this weirdo all over your TikTok and Instagram this week,

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.000
coming straight out of obscurity to generate millions of views across social media,

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:15.340
despite being an AI persona generated for the sole purpose of shilling a crypto meme coin,

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:23.980
which has purportedly already pulled in $4.6 million and spawned a legion of AI-generated

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.180
copycat accounts, funneling to their own pump-and-dump rug pulls,

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:32.520
Meaning the dead internet is no longer a theory, but a profitable reality.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.880
But what is reality?

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.380
Why even go to work?

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.140
And why even lock in?

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.600
When you can just passively pull in $26,000 an hour with an AI avatar throwing hands.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:48.200
In a game where the rules are made up so soon little content and few products will be real.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.480
And the mystery endures as to whether we're also dancing for some profiting puppet masters.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.740
In a nested slop simulation and its turtles all the way down.
